// check: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// CROWN — latency rides the RESUME VALUE. A closure performing E, handed
// back out of an arm through `resume`, extracted and CALLED under `with
// !E`: the row must ride the continuation's answer to the call site.
// Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// The declared `with Pure` on the returned fn type is load-bearing and is
// the whole finding here. WITHOUT it the same program checks clean and
// RUNS (measured 2026-08-18, exit 7 with the outer handler answering),
// because an unannotated fn type in a return position mints a free row
// VAR, and a var is the effect-polymorphic flow channel rather than a cap
// to subsume under — so the arm teaches the declaration its row instead of
// meeting it. That gap is `Hβ.effects.return-position-fn-row-is-a-var`.
effect E { op() -> Int }

effect G { give() -> (() -> Int with Pure) }

handler eh { op() => resume(7) }

handler gh { give() => resume(() => op()) }

fn body() with !E = {
  let f = (give()) ~> gh
  f()
}

fn main() = (body()) ~> eh
